    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOH2Qg5s8AAAABEG7IuQ",
      "title": "README, AGENTS: note that the op-geth binary is end of life",
      "author": "geoknee",
      "number": 813,
      "body": "## Why\n\nNothing in this repository says the `op-geth` binary is end of life. The README is still the upstream go-ethereum one — it does not mention the OP Stack at all — so a node operator landing here has no way to learn that the binary will stop following the chain at the next fork, and an agent reading `AGENTS.md` will read the missing forks as a gap to fill.\n\n## What\n\nTwo docs, no code.\n\n- **`README.md`** — a `> [!WARNING]` banner above the upstream content: the binary is no longer a supported OP Stack execution client, it will not be updated for **L1 hardforks from Glamsterdam onwards** or **L2 hardforks from Karst onwards**, and a node running it stops following the chain at the first of those to activate. It also says why the repository is still here: other parts of the OP Stack consume it as a Go library, via the `replace github.com/ethereum/go-ethereum => github.com/ethereum-optimism/op-geth` directive.\n- **`AGENTS.md`** — the same status as the first section, phrased as instruction: do not implement those forks here, do not treat their absence as a bug, and say so when a task is really about the binary as a node implementation rather than the library.\n\nKarst today is config plumbing only — `IsKarst` and `KarstTime` appear in `params/config.go` and nowhere else — so the fork is declared but none of its protocol changes are implemented, which is consistent with what these notices now say.\n\n## Open question for reviewers\n\nThe README tells operators to \"move to another OP Stack execution client\" without naming one. If there is a recommended replacement to point at, say which and I will name it.\n\n## Testing\n\nDocs-only; no Go files changed, so the `AGENTS.md` pre-commit checklist (gofmt, `make all`, tests, lint, generate, baddeps) has nothing to act on.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/op-geth",
